.TH TOON-WRAP 1 "November 2026" "toon-mcp 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
toon-wrap \- PTY bracketed-paste wrapper that converts pasted JSON to TOON
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B toon-wrap
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
[\-\-]
.I COMMAND
[\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B toon-wrap
runs an interactive terminal command inside a transparent pseudoterminal (PTY)
proxy and intercepts bracketed-paste sequences (\fBESC [ 200 ~\fR ... \fBESC [ 201 ~\fR).
Standalone JSON payloads and embedded JSON objects or arrays inside pasted text
are automatically converted to compact TOON format before reaching the wrapped
application, provided the TOON output is smaller than the original JSON.
.PP
Non-interactive runs (when stdin or stdout is not a TTY) bypass the PTY and
directly \fBexec\fR the target command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-aggressive
Disable aggressive auto-abbreviation of domain-specific keys (\fB_custom_keys\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-pure\-only
Convert only when the entire paste is valid JSON; ignore embedded JSON blocks.
.TP
.BI \-\-min\-chars " N"
Minimum JSON block length in characters to consider for conversion (default: 60).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show summary of options and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TOON_WRAP_DISABLE=1
Bypass the PTY wrapper and execute the target command directly.
.TP
.B TOON_WRAP_MIN_CHARS
Override the default minimum JSON block size in characters.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR toon-mcp (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Maintained by Vikyek <https://github.com/Vikyek>.
